        continue;\n            }\n            try {\n              adapter(envelope, entry);\n            } catch (e) {\n              logDebug(\"Adapter failed\", {\n                destination: entry.destination,\n                error: String(e),\n              });\n              postMetric(\"adapter_failed\");\n            }\n          }\n        }\n        // --- end vendor adapters ---------------------------------------\n\n        // Envelope contract (v2, the resolved instruction):\n        // {event_name, event_id, event_timestamp, destinations} — the\n        // three strings non-empty and length-capped as before, and\n        // `destinations` a REQUIRED array (possibly empty, length-capped)\n        // of {destination, vendor_event?, value?, pixel_ids?} entries:\n        // destination a non-empty length-capped string (NOT validated\n        // against any vendor list here - adapters each look up their\n        // own name, unknown names are inert, and the executor's\n        // build-pinned pixel-id allowlist bounds what any entry may\n        // fire), vendor_event optional but a non-empty\n        // length-capped string when present (the config-declared ad\n        // network event name; absent = that adapter has nothing to\n        // fire and drops the entry),\n        // value optional but a finite number when present (absent =\n        // count-only), pixel_ids optional but a non-empty count-capped\n        // array of non-empty length-capped strings when present (absent\n        // = that adapter stays dormant; the bridge omits the field\n        // rather than send an empty list, so an empty array is itself a\n        // never-produced shape). A malformed envelope - missing or\n        // non-array destinations, a bad entry shape, a bad\n        // vendor_event, a non-finite value, a bad pixel_ids list - is\n        // rejected whole: the\n        // parent-side bridge never produces those shapes, so they can\n        // only be forged or corru